  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::MuseumExhibit
  title: International Space Station
  meta: "First module launched November 1998  \xB7  Continuously crewed since November
    2000"
  body: The ISS is a laboratory the size of a football field orbiting about 400 km
    above Earth, built by the USA, Russia, Europe, Japan and Canada. People have
    lived on board without a break since 2000, testing how bodies, plants and machines
    cope with months in weightlessness.
  themeLink: 'The station is humanity''s rehearsal room: the first place where living
    off the planet became a daily routine rather than a short trip.'
  credit: 'Model: "International Space Station" by Poly by Google, CC BY 3.0, via
    Poly Pizza. Simplified, not to scale.'
