--- !u!114 &2053263037
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 2053263035}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a8c78a3dc61624f33b78b8b42697355c, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::MuseumExhibit
  title: iPhone (1st generation)
  meta: "Apple Inc.  \xB7  Announced 9 Jan 2007  \xB7  Released 29 Jun 2007 (US)"
  body: "The first iPhone combined a phone, an iPod and an internet device in one
    slab of glass. Instead of a plastic keypad it used a 3.5-inch multi-touch screen,
    so the controls became software that could change after you bought it.\n\nWhen
    the App Store opened in July 2008, the phone began absorbing other objects: the
    camera, the paper map, the music player, the flashlight and eventually the wallet.
    Most people now carry this one object everywhere, and much of daily life \u2014
    directions, payment, photos, conversation \u2014 passes through it."
  themeLink: 'This is where our route begins: technology leaving the desk and moving
    into the pocket, onto the body, and finally off the planet. The cheap, tiny chips,
    batteries and sensors made for phones later flew in space (see mode 3).'
  credit: 'Model: "Smartphone" by smallbigsquare, CC0, via Poly Pizza. Generic smartphone
    shown at 5x scale, not an official Apple model.'
  interactPoint: {fileID: 0}
  interactRange: 3
  model: {fileID: 1522014536}
  sway: 1
  swayAngle: 28
  screen: {fileID: 1767828466}
  focusHighlight: {fileID: 2987141}
  keepModeOnOpen: 0
  onModeChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  musicSource: {fileID: 0}
  modes:
  - label: "2007 \xB7 Glass replaces keys"
    caption: A single touchscreen replaced the keypad. Buttons became pictures that
      software could redraw at any time.
    screenColor: {r: 0.25490198, g: 0.9137255, b: 0.92156863, a: 1}
    showObject: {fileID: 0}
    lift: 0
    spinSpeed: 14
    music: {fileID: 0}
  - label: "2008 \xB7 Apps absorb objects"
    caption: With the App Store, one device swallowed the camera, map, music player
      and wallet now floating around it.
    screenColor: {r: 0.67058825, g: 0.4509804, b: 1, a: 1}
    showObject: {fileID: 61564907}
    lift: 0
    spinSpeed: 30
    music: {fileID: 0}
  - label: "2013 \xB7 A phone in orbit"
    caption: NASA's PhoneSat missions (2013) flew off-the-shelf smartphones as the
      computers of tiny satellites. Pocket tech became space hardware.
    screenColor: {r: 1, g: 0.49803922, b: 0.78431374, a: 1}
    showObject: {fileID: 483287817}
    lift: 0.35
    spinSpeed: 45
    music: {fileID: 0}
